Check overlaps: swing right 58 bottom 58 72x72 => x right 58..130, y bottom 58..130. rescue right 122..172, y 98..148 -> overlaps swing region horizontally x 122..130 and vertically 98..130. Slight overlap 8x32. Move rescue to right 0 bottom 168? Action zone 176; button would be above web (right 0 bottom 86..145) with bottom 168..218, outside zone. Hmm.

Let's redesign mobile actions as a clean cross:
- swing: right 52 bottom 52, 72x72 (center-ish)
- web: right 0 bottom 96 (top-right)
- strike: right 0 bottom 8 (bottom-right)
- dodge: right 124 bottom 8 (bottom-left)
- rescue: right 124 bottom 96 (top-left)
This is a 2x2 + big center? Actually swing overlaps with all at center. Coordinates: action area 176x176.
  swing right 52, bottom 52, size72 => occupies x 52..124, y 52..124.
  web right 0, bottom 96, size59 => x 117..176, y 96..155. Overlaps swing x 117..124 (7px) y 96..124 (28px).
  strike right 0, bottom 8 => x117..176 y8..67; overlaps swing x117..124 y52..67.
  dodge right 124 bottom 8 => x -7..52 y8..67; touches swing x52 at edge.
  rescue right 124 bottom 96 => x -7..52 y96..155; touches swing at x52 edge.
Slight overlaps are normal among round buttons; visually might be okay. But hit areas overlap at edges. Could make swing 64x64 and positions better:
  swing right 56 bottom 56 64 => x56..120 y56..120.
  web right 0 bottom 100 56 => x120..176 y100..156.
  strike right 0 bottom 12 56 => x120..176 y12..68.
  dodge right 120 bottom 12 56 => x0..56? 176-120-56=0 y12..68.
  rescue right 120 bottom 100 56 => x0..56 y100..156.
Perfect grid: 2x2 corners + center. Use size 56 for all. But swing 64 could touch. Let's set swing 62 at right 57 bottom 57 => x57..119, y57..119. Corner buttons 54 at right 0/122 bottom 122/0? Top-right x122..176 y122..176; top-left x0..54 y122..176; bottom-right x122..176 y0..54; bottom-left x0..54 y0..54. Then swing center x57..119 y57..119, no overlaps, gaps 3px. But action area 176 high, buttons top at 176 which is fine. Rescue top-left. All visible.

