```

Now hero landed on the street? He's in the middle of a road (crosswalk), and the goblin is 119m away. How did the player end up on the street? The strike zipped to Goblin at height 121? Then fell to street (y=0). That's okay if the strike knocks him down; but it should keep him in the air/swinging. After strike, velocity set and y velocity +3.5, but he may fall. The goblin now 119m. The city street is visible with crosswalk, car lights, but no cars? There is a red car at far left. The street looks flat purple/dark. This is playable but the chase resets far.

However gameplay issue: after a strike, the Goblin keeps flying; player lands on street and must re-swing. That's acceptable, but the player should be able to swing from street. Can the web attach from ground? `tryAttachWeb` picks anchors; buildings at 66+ high, from street within range maybe. The web anchor search range? Let's test pressing space from street to see if he swings. Also he might be stuck because buildings sides.

More critical: the goblin distance increased 119m after 2 sec from 7m? Because the strike dash teleports player to target but goblin speed maybe set 0; but distance 119 means the player fell way down to street, goblin stayed at 121 height. Vertical distance alone ~119. Yes. So the player must swing back up. That's fine.

The city street is quite empty (no cars because traffic lanes maybe x ±24, and player at x 0? Cars move along z, but few). Could add more cars/street lights. But not essential.

The reticle remains visible with green target even though Goblin 119m (<135) and not visible. It's at hero center again, overlapping his head. Because target in range. Hmm. The reticle fixed center still looks like a green circle on hero. Maybe only show reticle when the Goblin is on-screen and near the center of screen? Or remove reticle entirely and rely on web target marker. The reticle is supposed to be an aiming reticle, but without manual aim it's decorative. It creates a "target on hero's back" effect. Better hide it when target distance > 60 or when offscreen. Or reposition reticle to the Goblin's projected screen position! That would be ideal: make reticle track the target. `UI.showMarker` projects; we could add a reticle tracking method. But simpler: hide reticle when not within 45m. Or make it small and semi-transparent at screen center.

Let's implement reticle tracking: in updateUi, when inRange and goblin visible, project goblin screen pos and set reticle left/top; if on screen. When not target, hide. Then the reticle aligns with Goblin. But `setReticleTarget` only toggles class. We can extend signature `setReticleTarget(active, worldPos, camera)` and update position. However at 119m, goblin is behind buildings/off-screen, projecting maybe offscreen. We can hide if offscreen.

Simpler: remove target reticle from HUD entirely and use `markerWeb` (world marker with WEB label). That is already there and tracks screen position with clamping. The reticle adds a crosshair overlay only when within 135m. Could still be nice at close range. I'll repurpose: in UI, add `positionReticle(worldPosition, camera)` that projects and places reticle at screen point if on screen; otherwise hide. Show only when active. The reticle then circles the goblin. Update in `updateUi` after computing goblinPos.

Implementation:
```
setReticleTarget(active, worldPosition=null, camera=null) {
  this.reticle.classList.toggle('is-target', active);
